  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Expanding the business activities in Kenya, Rwanda and South-Africa.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&quot;With a DGGF Pre-finance loan Correctbook will be able to invest in further market development and implementation their &#x201c;Joy of Writing&#x201d;: 

a comprehensive bundled solution that includes erasable writing tools, teacher training, and impact monitoring, all integrated into their holistic approach.

Correctbook is a Dutch social enterprise that produces reusable, erasable notebooks, and accessories to reduce paper waste and promote sustainable writing. Their products include notebooks with erasable pages and special pens, designed for both personal and corporate use. 

Correctbook dedicates part of its revenue currently to fighting illiteracy in developing countries through its initiative, Correctbook Africa, which provides erasable writing materials and teacher training to under-resourced schools.

The Correctbook Africa initiative showed strong potential and represented a significant business opportunity, and a pilot was set up in 2025. Market research and validation were carried out with the support of DGGF Technical Assistance

For the next steps of expanding in Africa, the company developed a &#x201c;Joy of Writing&#x201d; business concept and additional funding is needed&quot;</narrative>
  </description>
